1
00:00:14,625 --> 00:00:17,125
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:47,375
MIRACLES OF THE ER

3
00:00:51,125 --> 00:00:53,249
Mr. Wei, are you feeling better?

4
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:54,832
[Mr. Wei sighs]

5
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,582
Yes, thank you.

6
00:00:56,583 --> 00:00:58,415
Do you want some water, Dad?

7
00:00:58,416 --> 00:00:59,625
[Mr. Wei coughs]

8
00:01:00,208 --> 00:01:02,624
He's doing better.
But my dad keeps coughing.

9
00:01:02,625 --> 00:01:04,791
He's lost some lung capacity.

10
00:01:05,041 --> 00:01:06,416
What if he can't sing?

11
00:01:06,958 --> 00:01:08,082
[Mr. Wei sighs]

12
00:01:08,083 --> 00:01:11,333
Mr. Wei, you don't need
to worry about anything.

13
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:14,665
Just get well
and leave the hospital matters to me.

14
00:01:14,666 --> 00:01:17,750
I'll make sure
they'll be paying for all your losses.

15
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:20,583
I'm glad you're here
to help guide us through this.

16
00:01:21,083 --> 00:01:23,208
Don't worry. It's what I do.

17
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:28,124
There's that doctor, Lin Geng-ming.

18
00:01:28,125 --> 00:01:30,332
- Did he still come visit you?
- Oh.

19
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:33,375
I don't think he'll come back again.
I really laid into him.

20
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:35,999
He knows there's medical negligence.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,458
He's acting nice
in hopes you'll drop the lawsuit.

22
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:41,290
No matter what he does,
you must ignore him.

23
00:01:41,291 --> 00:01:42,583
No contact at all.

24
00:01:43,083 --> 00:01:44,082
Okay.

25
00:01:44,083 --> 00:01:45,499
Did you hear that, Dad?

26
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,333
If that doctor comes to see you again,
call me at once.

27
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:51,375
[indistinct conversations]

28
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:55,665
Ms. Yang?

29
00:01:55,666 --> 00:01:57,957
- Hi. What are you doing here?
- [Geng-ming chuckles]

30
00:01:57,958 --> 00:01:59,458
Oh. Uh, right.

31
00:02:01,166 --> 00:02:05,000
I'm an Emergency Physician,
but I'm just an R1. [laughs]

32
00:02:07,625 --> 00:02:08,957
[Ms. Yang exhales]

33
00:02:08,958 --> 00:02:11,500
I really didn't expect
that you would go this far.

34
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:14,082
Oh. Wait, what are you talking about?

35
00:02:14,083 --> 00:02:16,541
Dr. Lin Geng-ming, I'm warning you,

36
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,499
do not approach
this client or me in private again.

37
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,499
My client won't withdraw the lawsuit.

38
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,082
You'll have to pay
every cent of compensation

39
00:02:24,083 --> 00:02:26,332
for financial and emotional damages.

40
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:29,290
- Y-you're Wei Sung's lawyer?
- [sighs] Dr. Lin.

41
00:02:29,291 --> 00:02:30,499
Leave this to me.

42
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,624
You should go.

43
00:02:31,625 --> 00:02:33,290
First, I should explain myself--

44
00:02:33,291 --> 00:02:36,000
[sternly] I said, let me handle this.

45
00:02:38,416 --> 00:02:41,291
Ms. Yang, I'll take you
to the conference room. This way.

46
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:47,708
- [footsteps departing]
- [Geng-ming sighs]

47
00:02:50,291 --> 00:02:51,708
[Geng-ming sighs]

48
00:02:53,625 --> 00:02:55,375
What you doing? Having a break?

49
00:02:57,416 --> 00:03:00,957
Dr. Chiu, how do you cope
with work-related stress?

50
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:02,625
You messed up with a patient?

51
00:03:03,041 --> 00:03:04,040
[Geng-ming] Mm.

52
00:03:04,041 --> 00:03:06,457
You currently feel
tightness in your chest?

53
00:03:06,458 --> 00:03:08,874
Lethargy? Dizziness, nausea?

54
00:03:08,875 --> 00:03:10,166
[Geng-ming] Mm.

55
00:03:11,083 --> 00:03:15,165
Do you keep replaying what went wrong,
get a useless feeling

56
00:03:15,166 --> 00:03:17,500
and wish you could
go back in time and try again?

57
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:19,624
How did you know that?

58
00:03:19,625 --> 00:03:21,500
Don't worry about it. You're doing great.

59
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
What?

60
00:03:24,250 --> 00:03:25,625
No doctor's perfect, man.

61
00:03:26,166 --> 00:03:28,707
We all make mistakes.
You just gotta learn from them.

62
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:31,958
Geng-ming, you're already better
than you were yesterday.

63
00:03:34,166 --> 00:03:35,374
[Geng-ming groans]

64
00:03:35,375 --> 00:03:36,499
[footsteps depart]

65
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,415
- [maracas rattling]
- [Geng-ming sighs]

66
00:03:38,416 --> 00:03:40,208
[siren wailing]

67
00:03:41,125 --> 00:03:43,540
[voice over pa system]
<i>Trauma Blue. ER, Trauma Blue.</i>

68
00:03:43,541 --> 00:03:45,707
- [suspenseful music playing]
- [Geng-ming panting]

69
00:03:45,708 --> 00:03:47,125
[Geng-ming] It's serious.

70
00:03:47,958 --> 00:03:49,875
- Resus room, hurry!
- [paramedic] Okay.

71
00:03:50,875 --> 00:03:52,957
[paramedics] One, two, three.

72
00:03:52,958 --> 00:03:54,332
[Yu-hua] How was he hurt?

73
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:57,124
[paramedic] A steel cable snapped
while the patient was washing a building.

74
00:03:57,125 --> 00:03:58,583
He fell from the seventh floor.

75
00:04:00,416 --> 00:04:02,499
And there's a pulse. Prep for intubation.

76
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,249
- Two IVs, a liter of saline.
- [Wen-chih] Okay.

77
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:06,083
- Draw blood for crossmatch.
- Got it.

78
00:04:06,916 --> 00:04:08,582
[EKG beeping]

79
00:04:08,583 --> 00:04:10,333
[blood squelching]

80
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:13,790
[exhales] Send for four units,
whole blood, O neg.

81
00:04:13,791 --> 00:04:15,000
[Hsiu-ju] Yeah.

82
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,916
[panting] Dr. He.

83
00:04:21,708 --> 00:04:23,458
Ultrasound. Hurry!

84
00:04:34,666 --> 00:04:36,041
Massive internal bleeding.

85
00:04:36,916 --> 00:04:38,875
Intubate. [sighs]

86
00:04:44,666 --> 00:04:46,583
It's full of blood. Suction. Now!

87
00:04:46,708 --> 00:04:48,208
[Geng-ming breathing heavily]

88
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,375
[EKG beeping continues]

89
00:05:01,208 --> 00:05:02,333
Enough.

90
00:05:07,375 --> 00:05:09,249
- I'll get the blood ready. Here.
- Okay.

91
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:11,082
[Geng-ming panting]

92
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:12,250
And done.

93
00:05:20,041 --> 00:05:21,665
[EKG beeping frantically]

94
00:05:21,666 --> 00:05:22,790
VF.

95
00:05:22,791 --> 00:05:24,457
[Geng-ming breathing heavily]

96
00:05:24,458 --> 00:05:26,416
[Yu-hua] Tang Hsi, charge to 200.

97
00:05:29,375 --> 00:05:31,165
[machine powers on]

98
00:05:31,166 --> 00:05:32,583
200. Clear.

99
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,166
[Geng-ming panting]

100
00:05:46,666 --> 00:05:48,041
[Hsi] It's been two minutes.

101
00:05:49,125 --> 00:05:50,540
Try again.

102
00:05:50,541 --> 00:05:51,957
[machine powers on]

103
00:05:51,958 --> 00:05:53,291
200. Clear.

104
00:05:55,333 --> 00:05:57,915
[Geng-ming breathing heavily]

105
00:05:57,916 --> 00:05:59,250
I have the blood.

106
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:02,041
One, two, three. Switch.

107
00:06:03,791 --> 00:06:05,833
[Hsi breathing heavily]

108
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,124
[Wen-chih panting]

109
00:06:08,125 --> 00:06:09,708
[Wen-chih] Epi, last one.

110
00:06:12,083 --> 00:06:13,249
[Yu-hua sighs]

111
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:14,500
Done.

112
00:06:19,041 --> 00:06:21,540
[Geng-ming and Hsi]
One, two, three. Switch.

113
00:06:21,541 --> 00:06:23,625
[Geng-ming panting]

114
00:06:25,458 --> 00:06:27,166
[Hsi breathing heavily]

115
00:06:31,166 --> 00:06:33,041
[Geng-ming breathing heavily]

116
00:06:34,166 --> 00:06:35,500
Stop CPR.

117
00:06:36,375 --> 00:06:37,916
[heavy breathing continues]

118
00:06:38,416 --> 00:06:39,791
[loudly] Stop CPR.

119
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,583
[EKG flatlining]

120
00:06:47,458 --> 00:06:49,125
[Geng-ming breath trembling]

121
00:06:52,125 --> 00:06:53,750
[Hsiu-ju sighs]

122
00:06:56,083 --> 00:06:58,249
[sighs] Time of death,

123
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,457
let's call it.

124
00:06:59,458 --> 00:07:00,540
Dr. He.

125
00:07:00,541 --> 00:07:02,375
[EKG faintly beeping]

126
00:07:05,833 --> 00:07:06,958
What's that?

127
00:07:13,916 --> 00:07:16,458
Mr. Wang, we tried our best.

128
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:19,415
We'll get your family
to come see you later.

129
00:07:19,416 --> 00:07:20,957
I hope you rest in peace.

130
00:07:20,958 --> 00:07:22,832
[EKG faintly beeping]

131
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,750
He still has a heartbeat, though.

132
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,540
I heard if a patient has PEA,

133
00:07:29,541 --> 00:07:31,708
it means they have unfinished business.

134
00:07:32,791 --> 00:07:34,999
Might be waiting for his family.

135
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,040
Right. After his family comes,

136
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:38,333
let's see.

137
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,916
What are you planning?

138
00:07:46,416 --> 00:07:48,791
I... don't want them to see him that way.

139
00:07:49,666 --> 00:07:51,250
I'd like to stitch him up.

140
00:07:54,291 --> 00:07:55,541
[Hsi] I'll help you.

141
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:59,458
[bustling]

142
00:08:00,458 --> 00:08:01,624
Yu-hua?

143
00:08:01,625 --> 00:08:03,790
The family of that patient has arrived.

144
00:08:03,791 --> 00:08:05,125
Okay. Got it.

145
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,458
[Yu-hua sighs]

146
00:08:10,875 --> 00:08:12,500
He was 33.

147
00:08:13,125 --> 00:08:15,999
- [whining] I wanna go home.
- Mrs. Wang's over there.

148
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,790
We will, after we see your dad.

149
00:08:17,791 --> 00:08:19,957
- [daughter] I wanna go home!
- We'll go straight home.

150
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:21,040
[baby crying]

151
00:08:21,041 --> 00:08:22,875
I'm Dr. He from ER.

152
00:08:23,458 --> 00:08:25,290
I'm the wife of Wang Ming-i.

153
00:08:25,291 --> 00:08:27,957
And they said
that my husband is in the ER.

154
00:08:27,958 --> 00:08:30,040
Could I ask, is it serious?

155
00:08:30,041 --> 00:08:31,999
- Do you think I can see him?
- Uh...

156
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,165
[baby crying]

157
00:08:33,166 --> 00:08:34,458
I'm very sorry.

158
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,416
But your husband didn't make it.

159
00:08:39,208 --> 00:08:41,166
[Mrs. Wang crying]

160
00:08:43,166 --> 00:08:44,583
Impossible.

161
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:47,832
[baby wailing]

162
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,957
- Come on, let's go visit your dad.
- [Yu-hua] Oh.

163
00:08:49,958 --> 00:08:53,333
I'm sorry. Mr. Wang fell
from quite a height.

164
00:08:54,041 --> 00:08:56,290
It's not appropriate
for the kids to see him.

165
00:08:56,291 --> 00:08:58,457
But a nurse will take
good care of them. Here.

166
00:08:58,458 --> 00:08:59,916
I'll hold him for you.

167
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,250
[baby wailing continues]

168
00:09:08,166 --> 00:09:09,208
All done.

169
00:09:10,125 --> 00:09:11,375
[door opens]

170
00:09:11,916 --> 00:09:13,333
[Yu-hua] His family is here.

171
00:09:16,041 --> 00:09:17,916
[soft piano music playing]

172
00:09:19,125 --> 00:09:21,583
[Mrs. Wang breath trembling]

173
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:28,458
[sobbing]

174
00:09:32,625 --> 00:09:34,458
How did you do this?

175
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,416
[sobbing]

176
00:09:37,708 --> 00:09:39,083
[sniffles] You promised me

177
00:09:40,041 --> 00:09:41,874
you'd be okay.

178
00:09:41,875 --> 00:09:45,500
What should I do? I'm all by myself.

179
00:09:50,166 --> 00:09:54,999
[sobs] You promised me that you'd always
come home to me safely.

180
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,583
Tell me...

181
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:04,958
Our kids are so young still.

182
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:09,250
[EKG beeping]

183
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:11,165
[Mrs. Wang gasps]

184
00:10:11,166 --> 00:10:13,915
Doctor, doesn't he still have a heartbeat?

185
00:10:13,916 --> 00:10:15,791
That's just electrical activity.

186
00:10:16,291 --> 00:10:17,874
His heart isn't beating now.

187
00:10:17,875 --> 00:10:20,582
[wailing] He really still has a heartbeat.

188
00:10:20,583 --> 00:10:21,832
He's still alive.

189
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,290
Please, doctor!

190
00:10:23,291 --> 00:10:25,415
- I'm begging you!
- [Yu-hua] I'm sorry. Mrs. Wang...

191
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:28,082
- Please, I'm sorry. I'm...
- [Mrs. Wang wailing]

192
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:29,333
Please.

193
00:10:30,583 --> 00:10:32,290
[low bustling]

194
00:10:32,291 --> 00:10:34,665
- [Yu-hua] We can arrange all that.
- [Hsiu-ju] Let me--

195
00:10:34,666 --> 00:10:35,832
- [man] Doctor?
- Yes.

196
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:39,082
[man] Did you see a buckle
when you did that last resuscitation?

197
00:10:39,083 --> 00:10:41,832
Uh, what buckle is that?

198
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:43,415
It's a metal safety buckle.

199
00:10:43,416 --> 00:10:45,999
When working at heights,
you must always be secure.

200
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
- I didn't notice anything.
- [man sighs]

201
00:10:49,125 --> 00:10:52,333
Our company could only
claim insurance if he was wearing it.

202
00:10:53,041 --> 00:10:54,707
Ming-i was a hard worker,

203
00:10:54,708 --> 00:10:56,707
he was diligent. He must have fastened it.

204
00:10:56,708 --> 00:10:59,082
Could it have been
left behind at the hospital?

205
00:10:59,083 --> 00:11:00,333
Doctor.

206
00:11:01,291 --> 00:11:02,708
Please check for me.

207
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:09,541
[EKG beeping faintly]

208
00:11:14,416 --> 00:11:16,791
- [Geng-ming sighs] Dr. He.
- Uh-huh?

209
00:11:17,458 --> 00:11:19,999
- We've looked everywhere.
- Not here either.

210
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,540
[panting] Dr. He. The EMT searched
the ambulance, they didn't see it.

211
00:11:23,541 --> 00:11:26,291
And I also searched along the way
several times. [sighs]

212
00:11:30,583 --> 00:11:31,833
Could it be...

213
00:11:32,708 --> 00:11:33,750
in his body?

214
00:11:34,708 --> 00:11:36,875
You think it's inside of him?

215
00:11:40,583 --> 00:11:42,000
[Yu-hua inhales]

216
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:46,624
Let's search him.
The family might need the insurance money.

217
00:11:46,625 --> 00:11:48,749
If it's really in him, well then,

218
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:52,249
it wouldn't be fair
to blame him for negligence, would it?

219
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:54,166
- Yeah.
- [Yu-hua] Remove the stitches.

220
00:11:56,083 --> 00:11:57,916
[Mrs. Wang breathes heavily]

221
00:12:00,416 --> 00:12:02,416
[flesh squelching]

222
00:12:04,791 --> 00:12:07,041
[mournful music playing softly]

223
00:12:08,916 --> 00:12:11,041
[daughter] <i>Momma, is Dad okay?</i>

224
00:12:12,041 --> 00:12:13,790
Your father is busy.

225
00:12:13,791 --> 00:12:15,500
He won't be coming home.

226
00:12:16,541 --> 00:12:17,958
[shakily] But I'm here.

227
00:12:19,125 --> 00:12:20,541
[Mrs. Wang sniffles]

228
00:12:21,708 --> 00:12:23,583
[flesh squelching]

229
00:12:26,291 --> 00:12:27,875
[faint metal clinking]

230
00:12:28,291 --> 00:12:29,416
I've got it.

231
00:12:32,625 --> 00:12:34,125
[Geng-ming exhales]

232
00:12:35,458 --> 00:12:37,458
[Hsi and Geng-ming sigh in relief]

233
00:12:39,041 --> 00:12:41,540
Hsiu-ju, ask his wife to come back in.

234
00:12:41,541 --> 00:12:42,708
Sure, I'll get her.

235
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:49,791
Mrs. Wang, we found
your husband's safety buckle.

236
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,250
[Mrs. Wang cries]

237
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:01,333
[Mrs. Wang sniffling]

238
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:09,791
[sobbing]

239
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,583
You did good, my love.

240
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:19,290
It's been hard on you.

241
00:13:19,291 --> 00:13:22,750
You worked hard for us all. You have.

242
00:13:23,625 --> 00:13:25,333
[sobbing continues]

243
00:13:26,791 --> 00:13:29,666
Thank you for holding on for our sake.

244
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,583
[whimpers]

245
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:34,749
I promise
that I'll raise our daughters well.

246
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,708
It's fine, my love.

247
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:39,916
Rest in peace.

248
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,791
It won't hurt anymore.

249
00:13:46,791 --> 00:13:48,416
[EKG flatlining]

250
00:13:51,958 --> 00:13:53,583
[Mrs. Wang sobbing]

251
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,375
[Hsiu-ju sighs]

252
00:14:11,375 --> 00:14:12,957
Time of death,

253
00:14:12,958 --> 00:14:15,166
11:03 a.m.

254
00:14:18,041 --> 00:14:19,750
[bustling]

255
00:14:20,250 --> 00:14:21,833
[phone buzzing]

256
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:23,457
Siao Siang, what's up?

257
00:14:23,458 --> 00:14:25,457
[Siang on call] <i>Dr. Chou, did you see it?</i>

258
00:14:25,458 --> 00:14:27,374
<i>Dr. Huang published a new paper.</i>

259
00:14:27,375 --> 00:14:29,957
<i>His data is the complete opposite of ours.</i>

260
00:14:29,958 --> 00:14:32,415
<i>His patients' tumors
all shrunk significantly.</i>

261
00:14:32,416 --> 00:14:35,083
<i>Lung function
also shows significant improvement.</i>

262
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:39,208
<i>I really don't get it.
Why would our results differ so much?</i>

263
00:14:39,958 --> 00:14:42,291
Okay, I'm with a patient.
I'll call you later.

264
00:14:53,333 --> 00:14:56,624
Things are not going
as smoothly for Dr. Chou.

265
00:14:56,625 --> 00:14:57,999
I was quite worried.

266
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,208
But seeing such impressive data
in your paper now,

267
00:15:01,583 --> 00:15:02,666
I feel at-ease.

268
00:15:04,041 --> 00:15:05,957
Well, thank you for the opportunity.

269
00:15:05,958 --> 00:15:09,207
I have always been
so optimistic about you.

270
00:15:09,208 --> 00:15:10,790
Are you free on Friday?

271
00:15:10,791 --> 00:15:15,290
I'm having a meal with some
of the Board of Directors. Come along.

272
00:15:15,291 --> 00:15:17,707
Sure. Uh, thank you so much.

273
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,415
[Director] Chia-hsin will be there.

274
00:15:19,416 --> 00:15:21,999
I'll introduce you
so you can get to know each other.

275
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,374
- Huh?
- [You-chang] Mm.

276
00:15:23,375 --> 00:15:25,707
That's all. I won't keep you.

277
00:15:25,708 --> 00:15:27,083
Thank you, Director.

278
00:15:30,833 --> 00:15:32,583
[footsteps departing]

279
00:15:37,291 --> 00:15:38,624
- [knocks on door]
- Director?

280
00:15:38,625 --> 00:15:40,457
[Director] Cheng-chun, come in.

281
00:15:40,458 --> 00:15:43,040
Now, I'm guessing you must be worried.

282
00:15:43,041 --> 00:15:44,250
And stressed

283
00:15:44,666 --> 00:15:45,790
over your paper.

284
00:15:45,791 --> 00:15:47,083
[chuckles]

285
00:15:47,791 --> 00:15:50,207
Well, after reading Dr. Huang's work,

286
00:15:50,208 --> 00:15:52,041
- I'm not sure if I--
- [Director] Cheng-chun.

287
00:15:52,583 --> 00:15:55,624
Worries are self-inflicted, usually.

288
00:15:55,625 --> 00:15:59,666
Everything's simple if you know
when to continue and when to stop.

289
00:16:00,458 --> 00:16:01,541
What do you mean?

290
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:05,290
Currently, You-chang
has finished the paper on schedule.

291
00:16:05,291 --> 00:16:07,083
The effectivity is quite good.

292
00:16:08,333 --> 00:16:09,790
You take a break.

293
00:16:09,791 --> 00:16:11,540
Stop your research for now.

294
00:16:11,541 --> 00:16:13,291
It's decided then, hey?

295
00:16:13,875 --> 00:16:16,125
Focus on managing the ER.

296
00:16:18,583 --> 00:16:19,874
Oh.

297
00:16:19,875 --> 00:16:21,457
I've been meaning to ask you

298
00:16:21,458 --> 00:16:22,915
about Chia-hsin.

299
00:16:22,916 --> 00:16:24,666
How do you feel about her?

300
00:16:27,625 --> 00:16:29,000
[chuckles]

301
00:16:35,416 --> 00:16:36,916
[dial tone]

302
00:16:37,875 --> 00:16:39,666
[Director] Come here for a moment.

303
00:16:42,541 --> 00:16:44,500
I only have one daughter.

304
00:16:45,333 --> 00:16:47,416
Since she was little, I've doted on her.

305
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:51,457
Now, I only hope she can meet someone

306
00:16:51,458 --> 00:16:53,290
who truly cares for her,

307
00:16:53,291 --> 00:16:55,040
and have a good husband.

308
00:16:55,041 --> 00:16:57,166
[footsteps approaching]

309
00:16:58,833 --> 00:17:00,250
[knocks on door]

310
00:17:02,125 --> 00:17:04,500
- You're having tea with my dad.
- [Cheng-chun] Mm.

311
00:17:05,666 --> 00:17:06,916
Chia-hsin.

312
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,250
Dr. Chou has something to say.

313
00:17:12,416 --> 00:17:13,708
[Cheng-chun] Ms. Chang,

314
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:17,582
It's not possible for me
to meet with you privately.

315
00:17:17,583 --> 00:17:18,958
Please understand.

316
00:17:21,416 --> 00:17:23,583
[footsteps departing]

317
00:17:26,541 --> 00:17:28,332
What did you tell Cheng-chun then?

318
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:30,207
[inhales] Why would he say all of that?

319
00:17:30,208 --> 00:17:32,415
At the meal on Friday,

320
00:17:32,416 --> 00:17:34,916
I'll introduce you to Huang You-chang.

321
00:17:35,416 --> 00:17:36,708
He's very talented.

322
00:17:37,208 --> 00:17:39,291
And likely to take over my position.

323
00:17:39,833 --> 00:17:41,207
Why are you telling me?

324
00:17:41,208 --> 00:17:43,666
[gasps softly] Did you make
Cheng-chun say all that?

325
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,457
If Cheng-chun really liked you,

326
00:17:47,458 --> 00:17:49,750
I could never force him
to say that to you.

327
00:17:51,666 --> 00:17:53,125
I understand.

328
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:55,749
This is all to do with his paper, right?

329
00:17:55,750 --> 00:17:57,166
[elevator dings]

330
00:17:58,583 --> 00:18:01,457
Cheng-chun didn't give you
the data you wanted, did he?

331
00:18:01,458 --> 00:18:05,249
So you pushed him aside and chose
to support You-chang's paper instead.

332
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:07,250
And now you're playing matchmaker.

333
00:18:08,208 --> 00:18:09,832
You just have to trust in me.

334
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:11,790
I'm not doing you harm.

335
00:18:11,791 --> 00:18:13,249
[Ms. Chang sighs]

336
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:14,500
Dad?

337
00:18:15,166 --> 00:18:17,083
I'm really disappointed in you.

338
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:21,666
[Director] Pancreatic cancer, third stage.

339
00:18:25,166 --> 00:18:27,625
I was diagnosed three months ago.

340
00:18:28,250 --> 00:18:32,749
I've already asked Huang You-chang
to be responsible for my treatment plan.

341
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:34,540
[Ms. Chang's breath trembling]

342
00:18:34,541 --> 00:18:35,958
[Director sighs]

343
00:18:36,708 --> 00:18:38,583
[somber music playing]

344
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:40,541
Chia-hsin.

345
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:43,625
I don't have much time left, okay?

346
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:48,541
I need to arrange everything
on my way out.

347
00:18:49,083 --> 00:18:51,875
- [Ms. Chang cries softly]
- Including your happiness.

348
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:58,875
You are the one
that I'm most worried about.

349
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:02,625
[sniffles]

350
00:19:04,708 --> 00:19:06,875
[siren wailing distantly]

351
00:19:10,958 --> 00:19:13,083
[vehicles honking distantly]

352
00:19:17,458 --> 00:19:19,416
You're in a really bad mood.

353
00:19:20,458 --> 00:19:22,500
Is it because of You-chang's paper?

354
00:19:24,291 --> 00:19:27,083
[chuckles] It'll be... fine.

355
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:30,874
How about later we go...

356
00:19:30,875 --> 00:19:33,707
do a workout
and I can be your punching bag.

357
00:19:33,708 --> 00:19:36,208
But you can't hit me in the face. [laughs]

358
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:43,583
Today, I'll notify the team
to stop the research.

359
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:45,499
You mean that...

360
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,291
you won't finish your work?

361
00:19:47,833 --> 00:19:49,290
- [laughs sardonically]
- Why not?

362
00:19:49,291 --> 00:19:53,083
I can't think of a real reason
why I should finish it. [sighs]

363
00:19:53,625 --> 00:19:55,874
Just because your results
are different to him

364
00:19:55,875 --> 00:19:58,332
or do you think there's problem
with your research?

365
00:19:58,333 --> 00:20:01,040
Aren't you curious
why your data differs so much?

366
00:20:01,041 --> 00:20:02,541
[Yu-hua sighs]

367
00:20:04,041 --> 00:20:05,582
Cheng-chun!

368
00:20:05,583 --> 00:20:07,499
This isn't like you.

369
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:09,457
You choosing to give up now

370
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:12,165
will harm the patients
who are currently using the new drug.

371
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:14,749
- You know there's lives at stake.
- [Cheng-chun, sternly] Dr. He.

372
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,458
You're interfering.

373
00:20:24,083 --> 00:20:27,415
Everyone, I know
how hard you've all been working.

374
00:20:27,416 --> 00:20:29,707
- [residents agree]
- There's been a lot of overtime.

375
00:20:29,708 --> 00:20:32,040
But there are more challenges ahead of us.

376
00:20:32,041 --> 00:20:34,832
So, I'm asking you
to hang in there for a bit longer.

377
00:20:34,833 --> 00:20:37,999
- [residents agree]
- This weekend, you rest. Today, celebrate.

378
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,082
Cheers.

379
00:20:39,083 --> 00:20:43,166
[residents] Cheers. Thank you, Dr. Huang.

380
00:20:43,875 --> 00:20:46,915
Mm. I should get going,
Dr. Cheng is looking for me.

381
00:20:46,916 --> 00:20:49,082
- Okay.
- Thanks, Dr. Huang.

382
00:20:49,083 --> 00:20:50,915
[female resident] Congratulations.

383
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:53,165
[indistinct excited chatter]

384
00:20:53,166 --> 00:20:54,541
Dr. Huang?

385
00:20:55,416 --> 00:20:57,374
Oh. [chuckles]

386
00:20:57,375 --> 00:21:00,082
I thought you wouldn't come
'cause you have work today.

387
00:21:00,083 --> 00:21:02,957
[hesitantly] I have a favor to ask.

388
00:21:02,958 --> 00:21:04,374
Yeah. Go ahead.

389
00:21:04,375 --> 00:21:07,707
The patient with lung adenocarcinoma,

390
00:21:07,708 --> 00:21:11,874
was there a possibility he could join
the clinical trial for the new drug?

391
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:13,374
[You-chang sighs]

392
00:21:13,375 --> 00:21:15,708
You know that the slots
are all filled, right?

393
00:21:17,083 --> 00:21:18,207
[Hsi] Mm.

394
00:21:18,208 --> 00:21:20,875
[You-chang] Did the patient
ask you for this favor?

395
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:24,749
Doctors must learn to say no sometimes.

396
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,999
No. [stutters]
It's just the patient is a single parent.

397
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,415
<i>He has to set up his stall
and raise his kid.</i>

398
00:21:30,416 --> 00:21:33,124
<i>If he doesn't get treatment,
he won't last long at all.</i>

399
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,833
I'm the one that wants to help him.

400
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:39,083
[mellow music playing]

401
00:21:40,208 --> 00:21:41,291
Okay.

402
00:21:41,958 --> 00:21:43,958
Give his information to my assistant.

403
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,832
I'll open up a slot.

404
00:21:45,833 --> 00:21:47,165
Yeah. [chuckles]

405
00:21:47,166 --> 00:21:49,790
- Thanks, Doctor.
- Mm-mmm. There's no need.

406
00:21:49,791 --> 00:21:52,958
You really care about your patients.
I'm glad I was right about you.

407
00:21:55,541 --> 00:21:57,500
- [You-chang] Mm.
- [Hsi] Thank you.

408
00:21:59,291 --> 00:22:01,250
[footsteps departing]

409
00:22:03,416 --> 00:22:04,749
Chun-ting,

410
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:06,207
will you have some water?

411
00:22:06,208 --> 00:22:07,332
I'm playing games.

412
00:22:07,333 --> 00:22:10,040
- Don't nag me. It's frustrating.
- Here. Just have a sip.

413
00:22:10,041 --> 00:22:13,333
[groans] Grandma,
you made me lose a round.

414
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:16,040
- [Hsi] Hello, ma'am.
- Oh, you're here.

415
00:22:16,041 --> 00:22:19,249
Your X-ray doesn't show any fractures
so I'll treat your wound.

416
00:22:19,250 --> 00:22:20,333
[Mrs. Li] Mm.

417
00:22:21,666 --> 00:22:23,124
I'll clean it first.

418
00:22:23,125 --> 00:22:25,625
- [Chun-ting winces] Hey.
- [Hsi] Almost done.

419
00:22:27,375 --> 00:22:29,041
- Ah.
- That hurts.

420
00:22:29,916 --> 00:22:33,040
- How did you hurt yourself?
- Fell off a motorbike.

421
00:22:33,041 --> 00:22:34,540
- A motorbike?
- [winces]

422
00:22:34,541 --> 00:22:36,332
You told me that you tripped over.

423
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:39,291
[sighs] That's because I had
to deal with that dumb dog.

424
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,583
- [Mrs. Li gasps]
- What dog?

425
00:22:42,416 --> 00:22:43,707
Well, let me show you.

426
00:22:43,708 --> 00:22:45,790
[chuckles] It felt so good.

427
00:22:45,791 --> 00:22:47,625
- [dog whining on video]
- Look here.

428
00:22:48,166 --> 00:22:50,457
I came in here last time
because this dog bit me.

429
00:22:50,458 --> 00:22:52,332
- Mutt. [laughs]
- [Chun-ting on video] <i>Little shit!</i>

430
00:22:52,333 --> 00:22:54,457
Bark more! You love to bark.

431
00:22:54,458 --> 00:22:57,374
- See that? See. Look.
- [video] <i>Are you still barking now?</i>

432
00:22:57,375 --> 00:22:58,499
[Wen-chih] Dr. Tang.

433
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:00,540
- [video] <i>... barking anymore?
-</i> [Chun-ting laughing]

434
00:23:00,541 --> 00:23:03,125
How do you have money to buy a motorbike?

435
00:23:04,416 --> 00:23:06,333
It's... It's a friend's.

436
00:23:06,916 --> 00:23:09,457
A friend? How will you pay him back?

437
00:23:09,458 --> 00:23:11,665
- Since you damaged his bike.
- [groans] You're annoying me.

438
00:23:11,666 --> 00:23:12,832
Stop it, it's fine.

439
00:23:12,833 --> 00:23:15,374
How will you pay him without any money?

440
00:23:15,375 --> 00:23:17,499
- [yells] Oh, come on, shut up!
- [Wen-chih] Sir.

441
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:19,207
Can you lower your voice?

442
00:23:19,208 --> 00:23:21,208
You're disturbing the other patients.

443
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,333
[whispers] Do you need me to help?

444
00:23:31,041 --> 00:23:34,290
Dr. Cheng, this is Li Chun-ting,
who abused a dog last time.

445
00:23:34,291 --> 00:23:35,832
Oh, what's wrong with him?

446
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:38,415
He dragged the dog who bit him
behind his motorbike and fell.

447
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:40,000
That's why he's back.

448
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,666
Looks like no fracture.

449
00:23:47,291 --> 00:23:50,665
- Is there anything else you wanted?
- He's abused an animal more than once.

450
00:23:50,666 --> 00:23:53,875
I think we should report him
or get a consult with psychiatry.

451
00:23:54,708 --> 00:23:56,040
[Shao-ching sighs]

452
00:23:56,041 --> 00:23:59,083
Dr. Tang, let me give you
some advice, okay?

453
00:24:00,750 --> 00:24:04,249
If you don't want to have a lawsuit
in the same way as Dr. He Yu-hua,

454
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:08,040
the less time you spend
with a problematic patient, the better.

455
00:24:08,041 --> 00:24:10,082
Send him to the ward, discharge him.

456
00:24:10,083 --> 00:24:12,874
As long as he's not your problem,
there's no problem.

457
00:24:12,875 --> 00:24:15,291
Didn't you see? It was really bad.

458
00:24:15,791 --> 00:24:16,958
I understand.

459
00:24:17,541 --> 00:24:20,416
You can't accept it just yet. It's okay.

460
00:24:20,875 --> 00:24:22,874
Just keep in mind what I told you,

461
00:24:22,875 --> 00:24:24,375
you'll thank me one day.

462
00:24:24,875 --> 00:24:26,041
[Hsi sighs]

463
00:24:28,375 --> 00:24:30,625
I've read Huang You-chang's paper.

464
00:24:31,291 --> 00:24:34,708
Chou Cheng-chun
is working on the same thing.

465
00:24:35,333 --> 00:24:39,000
Yet you went to do research
with You-chang. You're obviously smart.

466
00:24:39,583 --> 00:24:42,749
You know that it's in your best interest
to follow

467
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:44,416
the right doctor.

468
00:24:47,208 --> 00:24:48,749
[typing]

469
00:24:48,750 --> 00:24:50,957
[Chun-ting on video]
<i>Bark more, you little shit!</i>

470
00:24:50,958 --> 00:24:54,083
- <i>Yeah, keep barking.</i> [laughs]
- [dog barking]

471
00:24:55,625 --> 00:24:56,958
[Tung-yen sighs]

472
00:25:01,666 --> 00:25:03,708
I may not like Dr. Cheng

473
00:25:04,208 --> 00:25:05,874
but I do agree with him.

474
00:25:05,875 --> 00:25:07,708
If you report this,

475
00:25:08,416 --> 00:25:10,707
Li Chun-ting
may hold a grudge against you.

476
00:25:10,708 --> 00:25:13,457
Then... follow you home someday,

477
00:25:13,458 --> 00:25:14,833
and attack you.

478
00:25:15,541 --> 00:25:17,708
It's better to just
mind your own business.

479
00:25:18,208 --> 00:25:19,458
I don't agree.

480
00:25:20,583 --> 00:25:23,040
This is about more
than just the physical wounds.

481
00:25:23,041 --> 00:25:25,165
If he has psychological problems,

482
00:25:25,166 --> 00:25:27,165
how can we pretend not to see it?

483
00:25:27,166 --> 00:25:30,208
However, if you can't even treat
physical wounds,

484
00:25:30,708 --> 00:25:33,333
- then you can't comment on others.
- That's different.

485
00:25:36,416 --> 00:25:38,875
[Hsi sighs] I'll discharge him.

486
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:40,708
Dr. Cheng decided.

487
00:25:41,291 --> 00:25:42,999
I don't want to do anything unnecessary.

488
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,166
Tang Hsi.

489
00:25:48,333 --> 00:25:50,916
[panting] 298, 299...

490
00:25:51,416 --> 00:25:53,374
- [sing-song] I have lunches for you.
- ...300.

491
00:25:53,375 --> 00:25:55,207
Nice, I'm starving.

492
00:25:55,208 --> 00:25:57,416
- Yours is a bad-tasting one.
- [Hsiang-chun chuckles]

493
00:25:57,916 --> 00:25:59,749
That's a high-protein meal right there.

494
00:25:59,750 --> 00:26:02,124
- You wouldn't get it, chubby boy.
- I'd rather be fat.

495
00:26:02,125 --> 00:26:04,915
- What about you? Here.
- I got fragrant pork rib rice.

496
00:26:04,916 --> 00:26:06,249
- Thank you.
- [Wen-chih] Hsiang-chun,

497
00:26:06,250 --> 00:26:08,749
you know after 30,
your metabolism deteriorates.

498
00:26:08,750 --> 00:26:09,957
Ooh, good taste.

499
00:26:09,958 --> 00:26:12,916
- Who ordered the curry rice like me?
- I think that's...

500
00:26:14,916 --> 00:26:16,457
[Chih-cheng sighs]

501
00:26:16,458 --> 00:26:19,040
Hsiang-chun,
you better face me when you eat.

502
00:26:19,041 --> 00:26:22,415
Somebody's got a big frown on their face.
You might lose your appetite.

503
00:26:22,416 --> 00:26:24,707
Hsiang-chun, turn around and face me.

504
00:26:24,708 --> 00:26:28,041
Otherwise, you'll see someone
eating like a pig. You won't feel well.

505
00:26:28,791 --> 00:26:30,500
Uh, I forgot my protein.

506
00:26:31,083 --> 00:26:33,290
Hardworking staff, enjoy your meal.

507
00:26:33,291 --> 00:26:35,665
Hsiang-chun, it's not about
how you look when you eat,

508
00:26:35,666 --> 00:26:38,332
Some people mix their food
in a way a pig wouldn't eat it.

509
00:26:38,333 --> 00:26:40,540
[laughs sarcastically]
At least you admit you're a pig.

510
00:26:40,541 --> 00:26:43,874
Hsiang-chun, let me show you.
Curry rice is best mixed together.

511
00:26:43,875 --> 00:26:47,665
You ever seen anyone eat their noodles
separate from their soy bean sauce? No.

512
00:26:47,666 --> 00:26:50,665
Hsiang-chun, we're talking about rice
and she's talking about noodles.

513
00:26:50,666 --> 00:26:52,582
- How do you eat it?
- Say it, I'll support you.

514
00:26:52,583 --> 00:26:54,832
How do you eat your curry rice?
Do you mix it or not?

515
00:26:54,833 --> 00:26:57,791
- Tell us. Don't be scared at all. Hmm?
- Tell us. Come on, tell us.

516
00:26:58,958 --> 00:27:00,791
[playful music playing]

517
00:27:01,708 --> 00:27:03,290
I'm not hungry.

518
00:27:03,291 --> 00:27:04,666
I'll eat this later.

519
00:27:05,625 --> 00:27:07,499
You scared her so much she won't eat.

520
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:09,540
This is the reason we broke up
in the first place.

521
00:27:09,541 --> 00:27:10,832
You and your curry rice.

522
00:27:10,833 --> 00:27:12,375
- Unmixed.
- [Hsiu-ju scoffs]

523
00:27:13,875 --> 00:27:15,375
[indistinct chatter]

524
00:27:21,875 --> 00:27:23,666
Tung-yen, need any help?

525
00:27:24,458 --> 00:27:25,790
Of course not.

526
00:27:25,791 --> 00:27:26,875
Hmm.

527
00:27:27,958 --> 00:27:29,875
Oh! Chocolates.

528
00:27:31,166 --> 00:27:32,708
Is this from a girl?

529
00:27:33,208 --> 00:27:34,374
[Tung-yen] Yes.

530
00:27:34,375 --> 00:27:36,874
- [Geng-ming gasps]
- I drained Mr. Chou's fluids

531
00:27:36,875 --> 00:27:38,290
so his wife gave it to me.

532
00:27:38,291 --> 00:27:40,291
Oh, Mrs. Chou gave it to you.

533
00:27:40,791 --> 00:27:41,749
Why only you?

534
00:27:41,750 --> 00:27:44,583
[Tung-yen] You didn't help.
Why would she give you one?

535
00:27:47,250 --> 00:27:48,540
[siren wailing]

536
00:27:48,541 --> 00:27:50,624
[dispatcher on call]
<i>119. What's your emergency?</i>

537
00:27:50,625 --> 00:27:53,040
[woman on call]
<i>I need an ambulance, please. Right away.</i>

538
00:27:53,041 --> 00:27:55,790
[crying] <i>My husband
is in a bathtub full of blood.</i>

539
00:27:55,791 --> 00:27:58,499
<i>I can't wake him up.
I don't know what to do.</i>

540
00:27:58,500 --> 00:28:01,832
[dispatcher] <i>Ma'am, don't panic.
We'll send an ambulance over right away.</i>

541
00:28:01,833 --> 00:28:03,125
[siren wailing]

542
00:28:03,875 --> 00:28:05,790
[paramedic panting]

543
00:28:05,791 --> 00:28:07,540
[paramedic] We've got an OHCA. Hurry!

544
00:28:07,541 --> 00:28:09,500
[Hsiang-chun] Get him to the resus room.

545
00:28:10,208 --> 00:28:12,083
Mr. Chou! How did this happen?

546
00:28:13,791 --> 00:28:15,250
One, two, three.

547
00:28:15,750 --> 00:28:17,499
- [paramedic] Mrs. Chou went for a walk.
- Su-ching.

548
00:28:17,500 --> 00:28:19,915
[paramedic] She came early
because she felt something was off.

549
00:28:19,916 --> 00:28:22,499
Found him lying in the bathtub
bleeding heavily from the wrist.

550
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:24,624
Looks like
he swallowed a lot of pills, too.

551
00:28:24,625 --> 00:28:25,916
I'll leave him to you.

552
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,499
- All right, prep for intubation.
- Yep.

553
00:28:28,500 --> 00:28:30,040
Su-ching, another IV.

554
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:31,624
- Okay.
- Epi, one every three minutes.

555
00:28:31,625 --> 00:28:34,790
- Epi, one milligram, IV push. Done.
- [Tung-yen] Okay.

556
00:28:34,791 --> 00:28:36,500
- Ready for intubation.
- [Tung-yen] Okay.

557
00:28:38,666 --> 00:28:40,250
[EKG beeping]

558
00:28:41,083 --> 00:28:42,708
Stop CPR.

559
00:28:44,375 --> 00:28:45,666
He signed a DNR.

560
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,666
[Tung-yen breathing heavily]

561
00:28:50,875 --> 00:28:52,582
[echoing] Oh, it's a relief.

562
00:28:52,583 --> 00:28:55,207
- It feels so much better.
- Here, Doctor.

563
00:28:55,208 --> 00:28:57,207
- Thank you. Thank you.
- [Mr. Chou chuckles]

564
00:28:57,208 --> 00:28:58,624
Don't be shy.

565
00:28:58,625 --> 00:29:00,625
- [EKG beeping]
- [Tung-yen panting]

566
00:29:02,041 --> 00:29:03,583
[Shao-ching, sternly] Take the tube out.

567
00:29:05,416 --> 00:29:08,790
The patient agreed to that DNR
because of his cancer.

568
00:29:08,791 --> 00:29:11,999
This situation,
it's not a product of his cancer.

569
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,540
- So it doesn't apply here.
- You can't know that.

570
00:29:14,541 --> 00:29:15,791
Take it out!

571
00:29:17,750 --> 00:29:20,374
And if we don't try
and we cause his death,

572
00:29:20,375 --> 00:29:22,249
then they sue us later,

573
00:29:22,250 --> 00:29:24,999
Dr. Cheng, will you take responsibility?

574
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:27,249
I'm a doctor.
I can't let him die in front of me.

575
00:29:27,250 --> 00:29:28,624
I'm doing my job.

576
00:29:28,625 --> 00:29:30,208
[EKG beeping rapidly]

577
00:29:30,375 --> 00:29:32,208
Okay. Okay.

578
00:29:36,208 --> 00:29:37,624
Tung-yen.

579
00:29:37,625 --> 00:29:39,207
Your job is to help.

580
00:29:39,208 --> 00:29:41,290
But it doesn't mean you have the right

581
00:29:41,291 --> 00:29:43,375
to make decisions for the patient.

582
00:29:45,500 --> 00:29:47,625
[rapid beeping continues]

583
00:29:52,250 --> 00:29:53,416
[sighs]

584
00:29:55,291 --> 00:29:57,666
His pulse is back. What should we do now?

585
00:29:58,375 --> 00:30:00,416
[Hsiang-chun breathing heavily]

586
00:30:02,583 --> 00:30:03,833
Finish your work.

587
00:30:05,208 --> 00:30:06,916
I'll take responsibility.

588
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:10,958
He's regained spontaneous breathing.

589
00:30:14,541 --> 00:30:16,790
[Mrs. Chou] Darling, I'm right here, okay?

590
00:30:16,791 --> 00:30:19,166
I hope you're feeling comfortable.

591
00:30:20,125 --> 00:30:21,583
[indistinct chatter]

592
00:30:22,666 --> 00:30:23,875
Mrs. Chou.

593
00:30:24,625 --> 00:30:25,999
Dr. Chiang.

594
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:29,874
When there's an available bed in the ICU,
we'll transfer Mr. Chou.

595
00:30:29,875 --> 00:30:31,582
Just wait a little longer.

596
00:30:31,583 --> 00:30:34,291
Dr. Chiang, any idea when he'll wake up?

597
00:30:34,875 --> 00:30:37,332
Well, his condition is stable for now.

598
00:30:37,333 --> 00:30:38,374
Yeah.

599
00:30:38,375 --> 00:30:41,332
But because... he lost a lot of blood,

600
00:30:41,333 --> 00:30:44,208
- and his brain was deprived from oxygen...
- Uh-huh.

601
00:30:45,416 --> 00:30:47,291
it's hard to determine his future.

602
00:30:49,166 --> 00:30:51,416
Is it possible that he won't?

603
00:30:52,541 --> 00:30:53,833
He won't wake up?

604
00:30:54,333 --> 00:30:55,541
[breath trembling]

605
00:31:01,416 --> 00:31:03,166
He has been sick

606
00:31:03,916 --> 00:31:05,458
for so long, you see.

607
00:31:06,791 --> 00:31:09,790
We have no money for treatment anymore.

608
00:31:09,791 --> 00:31:11,165
[cries softly]

609
00:31:11,166 --> 00:31:12,708
He's always...

610
00:31:13,458 --> 00:31:15,458
in pain. So he...

611
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:18,750
sometimes asks you to drain his fluid.

612
00:31:19,375 --> 00:31:22,208
To make it more comfortable. [cries]

613
00:31:25,375 --> 00:31:27,083
He even told me

614
00:31:28,125 --> 00:31:30,458
he didn't want to bring me down.

615
00:31:31,750 --> 00:31:33,500
[whimpering]

616
00:31:34,375 --> 00:31:36,833
Now he turned out this way.

617
00:31:37,833 --> 00:31:41,875
Honey, you left... you left me alone.

618
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,583
[sobs] <i>If I hadn't gone out today,</i>

619
00:31:47,750 --> 00:31:49,875
<i>this wouldn't have happened.</i>

620
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,458
Talk to me.

621
00:31:57,250 --> 00:31:58,958
[sobbing]

622
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:01,499
Speak... speak...

623
00:32:01,500 --> 00:32:03,040
Please speak.

624
00:32:03,041 --> 00:32:05,000
What should I do now?

625
00:32:05,583 --> 00:32:08,125
What do you want me to do? [sobs]

626
00:32:15,125 --> 00:32:16,791
[sniffles]

627
00:32:20,625 --> 00:32:22,416
[Cheng-chun]
I know you want to save people.

628
00:32:24,041 --> 00:32:25,332
But more than that,

629
00:32:25,333 --> 00:32:27,458
our job as doctors

630
00:32:27,916 --> 00:32:29,125
is easing their pain.

631
00:32:31,166 --> 00:32:33,332
[shakily] So I just have to let them die?

632
00:32:33,333 --> 00:32:35,208
Can I still be a doctor?

633
00:32:38,125 --> 00:32:39,666
Knowing when to let go

634
00:32:40,583 --> 00:32:42,332
is something you have to learn.

635
00:32:42,333 --> 00:32:43,833
It's not always easy.

636
00:32:46,083 --> 00:32:47,458
[Tung-yen sighs]

637
00:32:49,416 --> 00:32:50,916
[Tung-yen exhales]

638
00:32:56,291 --> 00:32:58,041
[plastic crinkling]

639
00:33:07,458 --> 00:33:08,875
[Tung-yen] What are you doing?

640
00:33:12,125 --> 00:33:13,041
Uh...

641
00:33:15,083 --> 00:33:18,290
It seemed like you were in a bad mood so...

642
00:33:18,291 --> 00:33:19,333
[Hsiang-chun inhales]

643
00:33:20,583 --> 00:33:22,040
[Tung-yen breathing shakily]

644
00:33:22,041 --> 00:33:24,000
[soft piano music playing]

645
00:33:26,375 --> 00:33:28,000
[plastic crinkling]

646
00:33:31,250 --> 00:33:32,416
Take it back.

647
00:33:33,708 --> 00:33:35,083
I don't deserve any of this.

648
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:46,041
[mournful music playing]

649
00:33:55,416 --> 00:33:58,708
Thank you for staying
to stitch up the body with me.

650
00:33:59,458 --> 00:34:01,333
I didn't stay because of you.

651
00:34:03,250 --> 00:34:06,040
[sighs] He decided not to let go yet.

652
00:34:06,041 --> 00:34:07,625
So, of course we couldn't either.

653
00:34:09,291 --> 00:34:11,458
I never used to believe
in things like that.

654
00:34:12,125 --> 00:34:14,375
I guess I never encountered them before.

655
00:34:15,458 --> 00:34:17,166
I used to not believe it.

656
00:34:18,500 --> 00:34:19,999
But since my mom passed away,

657
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:22,791
[inhales] I hope Gods,
ghosts, and the afterlife

658
00:34:23,416 --> 00:34:24,833
are all true now.

659
00:34:26,250 --> 00:34:28,333
[smacks lips] Maybe it means
I'll see her again.

660
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:29,750
[chuckles]

661
00:34:29,958 --> 00:34:31,125
I envy you.

662
00:34:32,541 --> 00:34:34,958
You can call your mom
whenever you think of her.

663
00:34:35,458 --> 00:34:37,208
You can hear her voice,

664
00:34:37,875 --> 00:34:39,082
and hang out.

665
00:34:39,083 --> 00:34:40,541
[chuckles softly]

666
00:34:42,291 --> 00:34:43,958
[bustling]

667
00:34:46,666 --> 00:34:47,916
Mom. [chuckles]

668
00:34:50,375 --> 00:34:52,999
- Hi there. I'm Lin Geng-ming.
- [Mrs. Tang exclaims]

669
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,374
Tang Hsi and I work together.

670
00:34:54,375 --> 00:34:56,624
He heard you're staying here
so he wanted to visit.

671
00:34:56,625 --> 00:34:58,541
- I couldn't stop him.
- [chuckles]

672
00:34:59,125 --> 00:35:01,915
[laughs] I heard you like food
so I brought you my favorite.

673
00:35:01,916 --> 00:35:04,249
- Barbecue the Cantonese way.
- [Mrs. Tang gasps]

674
00:35:04,250 --> 00:35:05,416
Here.

675
00:35:06,041 --> 00:35:08,540
Tang Hsi's never introduced
a boy to me before.

676
00:35:08,541 --> 00:35:10,957
- You're the first, you know.
- Oh, he followed me here.

677
00:35:10,958 --> 00:35:12,416
And we're colleagues only.

678
00:35:13,458 --> 00:35:16,332
She doesn't mean that.
She's always been strong-willed.

679
00:35:16,333 --> 00:35:17,874
You must be tolerant.

680
00:35:17,875 --> 00:35:19,415
- [Hsi] Mom!
- I got that.

681
00:35:19,416 --> 00:35:21,916
- [Geng-ming and Mrs. Tang laughing]
- Don't pretend.

682
00:35:22,916 --> 00:35:25,332
I can't remember seeing you smile so much.

683
00:35:25,333 --> 00:35:27,916
I'm about to lose my temper
because of you both.

684
00:35:28,541 --> 00:35:31,000
[chuckles, whispers]
Be careful of that temper.

685
00:35:32,291 --> 00:35:34,582
- [whispers] I will.
- Spoilt rotten.

686
00:35:34,583 --> 00:35:35,749
It's a good thing.

687
00:35:35,750 --> 00:35:37,500
Are you two done yet?

688
00:35:38,375 --> 00:35:39,332
Let's eat.

689
00:35:39,333 --> 00:35:40,791
[coughing]

690
00:35:48,041 --> 00:35:49,707
Mom, have some water.

691
00:35:49,708 --> 00:35:51,166
Here.

692
00:35:51,833 --> 00:35:53,500
[straining]

693
00:35:54,583 --> 00:35:55,625
Here.

694
00:35:56,625 --> 00:35:58,000
[swallows]

695
00:35:59,666 --> 00:36:01,375
[bustling]

696
00:36:04,291 --> 00:36:06,666
Hey. Why are you looking
at my mom's report?

697
00:36:07,250 --> 00:36:09,416
Oh... Do you think

698
00:36:09,958 --> 00:36:11,791
that your mom's coughing earlier was bad?

699
00:36:12,291 --> 00:36:13,750
No, it seemed the same to me.

700
00:36:14,541 --> 00:36:16,041
Did the tumor grow bigger?

701
00:36:16,916 --> 00:36:19,832
Well, Dr. Huang and I both
confirmed the CT results

702
00:36:19,833 --> 00:36:22,290
showed the size
of the tumor was controlled.

703
00:36:22,291 --> 00:36:25,374
And also, his paper
proved the drug was effective, didn't it?

704
00:36:25,375 --> 00:36:26,915
[sighs] Apparently.

705
00:36:26,916 --> 00:36:30,375
It will take some time
for the medication to work too, right?

706
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:32,041
I'm gonna go.

707
00:36:34,416 --> 00:36:36,458
[footsteps departing]

708
00:36:41,375 --> 00:36:43,290
[mouse clicks]

709
00:36:43,291 --> 00:36:44,832
[high-pitched ringing]

710
00:36:44,833 --> 00:36:46,833
[exhales]

711
00:36:49,875 --> 00:36:52,999
[Director, echoes] <i>Currently, You-chang
has finished the paper on schedule.</i>

712
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,749
<i>Stop your research.</i>

713
00:36:54,750 --> 00:36:56,457
[Yu-hua] <i>This isn't like you.</i>

714
00:36:56,458 --> 00:36:59,124
[Tung-yen] <i>So I just have to let them die?</i>

715
00:36:59,125 --> 00:37:00,957
[Jui's dad]
<i>You promised me you'd save him!</i>

716
00:37:00,958 --> 00:37:02,165
- [echo fades]
- [sighs]

717
00:37:02,166 --> 00:37:03,333
[knock on door]

718
00:37:03,916 --> 00:37:05,000
[Cheng-chun] Come in.

719
00:37:07,125 --> 00:37:09,540
- You're still at work?
- [Geng-ming] Dr. Chou.

720
00:37:09,541 --> 00:37:11,291
I want to show you something.

721
00:37:12,583 --> 00:37:13,958
Tang Hsi's mom's CT.

722
00:37:14,541 --> 00:37:17,415
Her results are significantly
different to Dr. Huang's paper.

723
00:37:17,416 --> 00:37:19,457
You're doing the same research.

724
00:37:19,458 --> 00:37:20,666
Is this normal?

725
00:37:24,583 --> 00:37:25,875
I'm not sure.

726
00:37:26,375 --> 00:37:27,540
[somber music playing]

727
00:37:27,541 --> 00:37:29,124
[Cheng-chun sighs]

728
00:37:29,125 --> 00:37:31,791
My research
indicates the drug doesn't work.

729
00:37:32,458 --> 00:37:35,124
It... But... Dr. Huang's published--

730
00:37:35,125 --> 00:37:39,207
From the data they provided, I chose
patients that had early-stage lung cancer.

731
00:37:39,208 --> 00:37:41,833
Maybe different stages
respond differently to this drug.

732
00:37:42,416 --> 00:37:44,750
Maybe... there's an error in my research

733
00:37:45,208 --> 00:37:48,250
- or something I missed.
- [Geng-ming sighs] But... [hesitates]

734
00:37:48,833 --> 00:37:51,374
Dr. Huang's research
could be wrong, right?

735
00:37:51,375 --> 00:37:53,874
[breathes heavily] It's quite late.

736
00:37:53,875 --> 00:37:55,374
- You should go home.
- But...

737
00:37:55,375 --> 00:37:57,874
Continue to follow up
on Mrs. Tang's condition.

738
00:37:57,875 --> 00:37:59,416
[sighs] All right.

739
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:05,500
[footsteps departing]

740
00:38:07,291 --> 00:38:08,833
- [exhales]
- [Geng-ming] Dr. Chou.

741
00:38:09,708 --> 00:38:13,125
If the drug isn't working,
it might harm a lot of people. So...

742
00:38:13,666 --> 00:38:14,791
don't give up.

743
00:38:16,708 --> 00:38:18,499
[embers burning]

744
00:38:18,500 --> 00:38:20,583
[ominous music playing]

745
00:38:24,666 --> 00:38:26,375
[music crescendoes]

746
00:38:29,750 --> 00:38:31,750
[closing theme music playing]
